      "writtenOn": "2024-07-18T12:56:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Could we just not call this at all ? And just keep the current task scheduled ?\n\u003e\n\u003e this.searchOptions was already updated and will be used the next time the task is \u003e sent, so maybe there\u0027s no need to do anything here ?\n\nAs discussed in the meeting, I simply rescheduled the time with the previous task, so the send query timing is the same as the previous task.\n\nIf we don\u0027t do anything here if there\u0027s another listener, but do schedule with backoff time if there isn\u0027t, the design will be a little more complicated and harder to follow.\n\n\u003e I guess the query mode etc. in the QueryTaskConfig might have changed, but we probably don\u0027t care ? A good refactoring would be to move queryMode, onlyUseIpv6OnIpv6OnlyNetworks, socketKey from QueryTaskConfig to QueryTask, so that QueryTaskConfig can contain only the query timing info (QueryTimingInfo ?).\n\nMade a change (aosp/3179740) to refactor `QueryTaskConfig` as you suggested.",
